Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789134065.5739138,"endTime":1789134082.0087402}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"frontend-design-pro","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v576nqg8ybkf0m3068vd6036sh8e73yz-JtLVnp/clawscan-skillspector-1168343431/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T13:41:04.192740+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":21,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":118,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4617,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3ea765f73ccc4616a23762446e34dc35","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.74,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest description is written entirely in Chinese and presents the skill behavior as Chinese-first without indicating that users may choose another language. Under the policy, forcing a specific language or locale without opt-in can be a natural-language policy violation.","remediation":"Add a statement that the skill can respond in the user's preferred language, or explicitly ask for or inherit the user's language choice rather than assuming Chinese.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":4,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-06224942ce9e4a95b2fa4d4a659f1b82","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7},"finding":null,"explanation":"The listed natural-language triggers include broad phrases like '优化界面' and '让设计更好看', which overlap with common user requests and can activate the skill unintentionally. This creates prompt-scope confusion: the assistant may apply hidden stylistic rules or rewrite code beyond what the user requested, reducing predictability and control.","remediation":"Replace ambiguous natural-language triggers with explicit opt-in phrases or slash commands. If natural-language triggers are retained, make them more specific, require strong UI/design context, and instruct the agent to confirm before activating when the request could be interpreted multiple ways.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-2fc8461f23c6402393c5ce5a54220d17","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":76,"end_line":76},"finding":null,"explanation":"The execution rule says the skill should activate for broadly defined 'design-related requests', which can cause unintended invocation in many ordinary frontend/UI conversations. Over-broad activation can override user intent, inject unsolicited constraints, and increase the chance that the model follows skill instructions when the user did not explicitly ask for them.","remediation":"Narrow activation conditions to explicit commands or clearly scoped triggers, such as requiring slash commands like /audit or /polish. Add disambiguation language that the skill should only engage when the user explicitly requests design review or improvement, and otherwise ask for confirmation before applying the skill.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":76,"end_line":76}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3145,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3159},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3132,"completion_tokens":426,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3558},{